# SYNOPSIS

```usage
false
```

# DESCRIPTION

`false` does nothing and exits 1.
Its arguments, if any, are ignored.

`false` is sbase's, and found only in the POSIX namespace: `/boot/bin/posix/false` is a hard link to `sbase-box`, which runs the command its name names, and `/lib/ns/posix` (a manifest's `ns=posix`, see namespace(6)) binds `/boot/bin/posix` before `/boot/bin` on `/bin`, so a POSIX program that runs `false` finds it there.
There is no native `false`.

# EXAMPLES

`tests/posix/sbasetest.c` runs `false` in the POSIX namespace and checks that it prints nothing and exits 1.

# SEE ALSO

true(1), test(1); sbase's page is `third_party/sbase/false.1` in the repository

# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit status is always 1.
